{"abstract":[{"text":"Mocking dependencies for SwiftUI Previews.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/factorykit\/previews"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Previews"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Factory can make SwiftUI Previews easier when we’re using View Models and those view models depend on internal dependencies. Let’s take a look.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"SwiftUI Previews","anchor":"SwiftUI-Previews","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s an example of updating a view model’s service dependency in order to setup a particular state for  preview.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ the view model","class ContentViewModel: ObservableObject {","    @Injected(\\.myService) private var service","    ...","    func load() async {","        let results = await service.load()","        ...","    }","}","","\/\/ the view","struct ContentView: View {","    @StateObject var viewModel = ContentViewModel()","    var body: some View {","        ...","    }","}","","\/\/ the preview","struct ContentView_Previews: PreviewProvider {","    static var previews: some View {","        ContentView()","            .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockService() }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If we can control where and how the view model gets its data then we can put the view model into pretty much any state we choose.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"SwiftUI #Previews","anchor":"SwiftUI-Previews","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same can be done using the new macro-based #Preview option added to Xcode 15.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockService() }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Multiple Registrations","anchor":"Multiple-Registrations","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There’s also a variant for Containers if you need to do multiple registrations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer {","            $0.myService.register { MockService() }","            $0.analytics.register { MockAnalytics() }","        }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Multiple Previews","anchor":"Multiple-Previews","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If we want to do multiple previews at once, each with different data, we simply need to instantiate our view models and pass them into the view as parameters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Prior to Xcode 15 and given the ContentView we used above, we’d need to do:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ContentView_Previews: PreviewProvider {","    static var previews: some View {","        Group {","            Container.shared.myService { MockServiceN(4) }","            let vm1 = ContentViewModel()","            ContentView(viewModel: vm1)","            ","            Container.shared.myService { MockServiceN(8) }","            let vm2 = ContentViewModel()","            ContentView(viewModel: vm2)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note the deprecated registration syntax."}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Of course, it’s even easier with #Preview as each one runs in its own context.."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockServiceN(4) }","}","#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer(\\.myService) { MockServiceN(0) }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the #Preview macro has been back-ported to iOS 13, there’s really no need to use the old syntax."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Common-Setup","text":"Common Setup","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If we have several mocks that we use all of the time in our previews or unit tests, we can also add a setup function to a given container to make this easier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension Container {","    func setupMocks() {","        myService { MockServiceN(4) }","        sharedService { MockService2() }","    }","}","","#Preview {","    ContentView()","        .withContainer { $0.setupMocks() }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"SwiftUI Previews","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FactoryKit"}]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Development and Testing","generated":true,"anchor":"Development-and-Testing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/SwiftUI","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Testing","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Contexts","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Debugging","doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Chains"]}],"references":{"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Contexts":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/contexts","abstract":[{"text":"Changing injection results under special circumstances.","type":"text"}],"title":"Contexts","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Contexts","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/SwiftUI":{"title":"SwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/swiftui","abstract":[{"text":"Defining and using dependencies in SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/SwiftUI","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Testing":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/testing","abstract":[{"text":"Using Factory for Unit and UI Testing.","type":"text"}],"title":"Testing","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Testing","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Chains":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/chains","abstract":[{"text":"Detecting and solving Circular Dependency Chains.","type":"text"}],"title":"Circular Dependency Chains","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Chains","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit/Debugging":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/factorykit\/debugging","abstract":[{"text":"Additional support for debugging resolution cycles, dependency chains and other issue.","type":"text"}],"title":"Debugging","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit\/Debugging","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://FactoryKit/documentation/FactoryKit":{"type":"topic","title":"FactoryKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A modern approach to Container-Based Dependency Injection for Swift and SwiftUI."}],"url":"\/documentation\/factorykit","identifier":"doc:\/\/FactoryKit\/documentation\/FactoryKit","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"}}}